{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Of the fowl after their kind, etc.</b> He should have put the beast first, if the verse orders them from above downward; and if from below upward, why did it order creeping thing after beast? And perhaps it is because the fowl possess an aspect of preeminence, for they are exceedingly numerous — go and deduce that the fewer among the birds are the unclean ones, and they are twenty-four, and they of blessed memory said (Ḥullin 63b) that there are one hundred kinds of birds on the Temple Mount and all of them are in the category of איה, and go and deduce concerning the clean ones, that they are manifold and manifold; whereas among beasts the fewer are the clean ones, ten [species], and they are not so numerous within each species as the birds. Therefore He commanded him concerning the birds first, for they are many, and he needed to bring of each and every kind in every detail; and afterward He mentioned the beast, for in its kinds it is few; and afterward the kinds that swarm upon the earth. Accordingly the verse ordered them by the order of the effort they require, from greatest to least."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:39:56.082014698Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}